# What must never reach the public site.
#
# Workers Static Assets uploads EVERYTHING under [assets].directory, and this repo's
# asset directory is its own root — so without this file the first automated deploy
# would publish package.json and the entire workers/ source tree at
# https://squidbay.ai/. The current hand-deployed site does not serve them (probed
# 2026-08-11: all 404). This file is what keeps that true once deploys are automatic.
#
# Patterns are gitignore-style. .assetsignore itself is never uploaded.
#
# NOTE for whoever edits this next: _redirects and _headers must NOT be listed here.
# Wrangler consumes them from the uploaded asset set, so ignoring them silently
# disables every redirect rule they define.

.git
.github
.gitignore
node_modules
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Repo machinery, not site content.
README.md
LICENSE
package.json
package-lock.json

# The Worker's own config, and the CI gates' input list. Both were reachable on the live
# site — retired-values.json answered 200 — which is config and process leaking onto a
# public marketing surface for no benefit to anyone visiting it. Neither is fetched by any
# page at runtime; the gates read retired-values.json from the Actions checkout, not over
# HTTP, so hiding it from the asset upload does not touch CI.
wrangler.toml
retired-values.json

# The chat Worker's source and config are deployed as a Worker, never served as files.
workers

# CI gates run in Actions; there is no reason for them to be downloadable from the site.
# This is the one intentional change from the current live boundary, which does serve
# design-system/ci/kill-list.mjs. Nothing in the site fetches these at runtime (checked).
design-system/ci

# A build tool, not site content. Run by a human to regenerate images/og/*.png; fetched by
# no page at runtime. It answered 200 on production until 2026-08-15 - the third file this
# denylist did not name.
design-system/og-template.html
